------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- ROW A1 (LEMMA 1), STEP 3:  RETAIN THE EXACT CANCELLATION BETWEEN THE
--   FOUR ORBIT REPRESENTATIVES BEFORE ANY INTERVAL ENCLOSURE.
--
-- PRIMARY SOURCES
--
-- Tadeusz Bałaban, "Renormalization Group Approach to Lattice Gauge Field
-- Theories. I. Generation of Effective Actions in a Small Field Approximation
-- and a Coupling Constant Renormalization in Four Dimensions",
-- Communications in Mathematical Physics 109 (1987), 249--301.
-- DOI: 10.1007/BF01215223.  Locators: Euclidean covariance (5.6),(5.7);
-- beta extraction (5.36)--(5.42).
--
-- Ludwig D. Faddeev and Victor N. Popov, "Feynman Diagrams for the
-- Yang--Mills Field", Physics Letters B 25 (1967), 29--30.
-- DOI: 10.1016/0370-2693(67)90067-6.
--
-- THE DEFECT THIS MODULE REMOVES.
--
-- `BalabanYM4LiteralWilsonFPHaarPositiveBetaExact` proves the one-sided orbit
-- gate by bounding the FOUR representative cell integrals SEPARATELY and then
-- assembling them with the hypercubic multiplicities (4,6,4,1):
--
--     R = 4 r1 + 6 r2 + 4 r3 + r4 ,       r_i >= - cellMeasure * epsilon
--   ==>  R >= - 15 * cellMeasure * epsilon .
--
-- The factor 15 = 4+6+4+1 is precisely the cancellation that was thrown away:
-- the four representatives are values of ONE joint Wilson + reduced
-- Faddeev-Popov + Haar density, and the estimate that the physics actually
-- supplies is a bound on the WEIGHTED COMBINATION
--
--     D(p) = 4 d1(p) + 6 d2(p) + 4 d3(p) + d4(p) ,
--
-- in which the Wilson, ghost and Haar pieces partially cancel against each
-- other AND the four orbits partially cancel among themselves.  This module
-- proves the gate directly from a bound on D, with no intermediate
-- per-orbit intervalization:
--
--     - epsilon <= D(p) for all p   ==>   R >= - cellMeasure * epsilon .
--
-- Everything the abstract cell functional has to satisfy is linearity
-- (additivity and rational homogeneity) plus monotonicity and the value on
-- constants -- true of any measure -- so nothing beyond `integral` being a
-- positive linear functional on the fundamental cell is assumed.
--
-- THE QUANTITATIVE GAIN, MACHINE-CHECKED IN SECTION 4.  For SU(2) in the
-- repository's normalized cube (cell measure 1/16) the admissible negative
-- sup norm of the physical density rises from
--
--     epsilon <= 44/45 = 0.977...        (one-sided, per-orbit)
-- to
--     epsilon <= 44/3  = 14.66...        (one-sided, cancellation-preserving)
--
-- exactly a factor 15, verified here as an identity and as a strict
-- inequality.  The user's step-4 target |4R1 + 6R2 + 4R3 + R4| <= 1/2 is also
-- discharged in the cancellation-preserving form: it holds as soon as the
-- COMBINED density obeys |D| <= 8 pointwise, again exactly.
--
-- WHAT IS STILL OPEN.  The physical leaf is unchanged in kind and strictly
-- weaker in content: one still needs the literal momentum-space joint
-- density of the CMP109 background-field vacuum polarisation and a bound on
-- the negative part of its (4,6,4,1)-weighted combination, uniform in cutoff,
-- volume and scale.  No such density exists anywhere in this repository, and
-- nothing below should be read as supplying one.  What is proved is that the
-- gate consumes fifteen times less than was previously demanded of it.
--
-- Exact rational arithmetic; no postulate, no hole, no receipt, no pragma.
-- Checked with `agda --safe`.
------------------------------------------------------------------------

